Automatically deletes attachments on post delete

== Description ==

Automatically deletes attachments (images, videos, files etc...) linked to a page, post or custom post type when it is deleted.


== Installation ==

1. Upload `auto-attachment-cleaner` folder to the `/wp-content/plugins/` directory
2. Activate the plugin through the 'Plugins' menu in WordPress
3. Select the post types on which the plugin should work on the page `Settings > Auto Attachments Cleaner` and save settings


== Frequently Asked Questions ==

= When are attachments deleted? =

When the post is permanently deleted from the trash or the trash is emptied


